    <string name="disclosure_title">Why the accessibility service is needed</string>
    <string name="disclosure_text">Take Your Brain uses the accessibility service (Accessibility API) to block apps according to your rules.\n\nWhat the service sees:\n• which app is open right now (its package name);\n• internal IDs of screen elements in apps where you blocked a part, such as the Shorts player in YouTube.\n\nWhat the service does:\n• counts the time while an app is open;\n• closes a blocked app and shows the block screen.\n\nThis data stays only on your phone. The app does not send or share it with anyone: it has no internet access. The service does not read or store texts, messages or passwords.\n\nBlocking will not work without the service. You can turn it off at any time in the phone settings.</string>
    <string name="disclosure_accept">I agree, open settings</string>
    <string name="disclosure_decline">Not now</string>
    <string name="privacy_title">Privacy policy</string>
    <string name="privacy_text">Date: October 30, 2026\n\nTake Your Brain helps you limit time in apps. All data is stored only on your phone. The app has no internet access: it sends nothing to us or to anyone else. There are no ads, analytics, accounts or cloud backups.\n\nAccessibility service (Accessibility API). It is needed to block apps according to your rules. The service learns which app is open (package name) and the internal IDs of screen elements in apps where you blocked a part, such as the Shorts player in YouTube. It does not read or store texts, messages or passwords.\n\nUsage statistics. With the Usage access permission, the app counts how much time you spend in apps. This is needed for limits, the time bank and statistics.\n\nWhat is stored on the phone: your rules, tasks and shopping lists, the block log (90 days), time bank accounts, daily results, settings, your name (if you entered it) and your PIN as a hash.\n\nNotifications and alarms are used for reminders and limit warnings.\n\nDeleting data. All data is deleted together with the app or with Clear data in the phone settings. You can turn off the service and permissions in the phone settings at any time.\n\nThe app is not intended for children under 13 and does not collect their data. If this policy changes, the new version will appear here and on the app page.</string>
